[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Use of Static Initialization Vector (IV) in AES Encryption. This issue arises because the code does not properly generate or manage the initialization vector (IV) for the AES encryption process. The IV should be unique and randomly generated for each encryption operation to prevent certain types of attacks, such as watermarking or known-plaintext attacks. If the same IV is used for multiple encryptions or if it is not securely generated, it can weaken the security of the encrypted data by allowing attackers to infer patterns or relationships between different ciphertexts.

